.TH LINEAR 1 2000-1月 "library_sizes" "library_sizes"
.SH NAME
library_sizes \- Get the implied library size of every training sample of the fitted network.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIlibrary_sizes(\fBmodel\fR as <generic> ElasticNet, 
\fBpseudo\fR as double = 1);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Get the implied library size of every training sample of the fitted network.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBmodel\fB \fR\- the perturbation engine that is created via \fBelastic_model\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBpseudo\fB \fR\- the pseudo count offset that was used by the log transformation, default 1. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a numeric vector, one value per training sample, i.e. \fBsum(2^x - pseudo)\fR of the
 expression matrix that was used to fit the network.
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
This vector is the bridge between an external raw count matrix and the model space:
 normalize the counts with \fBy = counts / sum(counts) * median(library_sizes)\fR and
 then apply \fBx = log2(y + pseudo)\fR.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
linear
.SH FILES
.PP
TRNtoolkit.dll
.PP
